<!-- faq -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="reveal center">
      <span class="kicker eyebrow">good to know</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Common questions</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <div class="qa reveal"><h4>Which do I install — app, Bridge, or CLI?</h4><p>On a Mac, the <b>Pounce desktop app</b> (a signed DMG). On Windows or Linux, the headless <b>Bridge</b> bundle. Or run <b>npx use-pounce</b> in any terminal — all three do the same job: host your agents and show a pairing QR. <a href="https://github.com/pounce-ai/pounce/releases/latest" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Get them here.</a></p></div>
      <div class="qa reveal"><h4>Phone and computer on different networks?</h4><p>Nothing to configure. Pounce opens its <b>own secure peer-to-peer tunnel</b> — pair once with the same QR and your phone reaches your machine over the internet. You can even <b>ssh</b> into a server, run <b>npx use-pounce</b> there, and pair it from anywhere. No VPN, no port-forwarding.</p></div>
      <div class="qa reveal"><h4>Is the connection secure?</h4><p>Each machine pairs with its own private token, and off-network access uses a direct peer-to-peer identity to reach home. There's no shared cloud inbox for your sessions.</p></div>
      <div class="qa reveal"><h4>What can it actually do?</h4><p>Stream every agent live, reply or redirect, approve permission prompts, and review diffs — then commit, push, or open a PR, all from the phone. See the <a href="/docs/getting-started">docs</a> for the full tour.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

